{"version":3,"_note":"Shared seed of the language\u2192docs registry \u2014 pure DATA, no language list in code. Every entry points at OFFICIAL LANGUAGE DOCUMENTATION (reference/manual/style guide), not linter rule catalogs: the AI reads the language's own docs \u2014 normative sections (deprecations, warnings, avoid/instead guidance) become rules, every code example feeds the what-is-normal reference corpus. A language may have several entries; all are learned and merged. Languages NOT listed are DISCOVERED on the fly (web search \u2192 crawl-validate) and cached per user in ~/.cache/helpers/lint-index/sources.json; share a discovered entry by committing it here (lint_submit).","registry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RockyWearsAHat/helpers/lint-models","sources":[{"tool":"rust-reference","language":"rust","kind":"crawl","seed":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/"},{"tool":"rust-api-guidelines","language":"rust","kind":"crawl","seed":"https://rust-lang.github.io/api-guidelines/"},{"tool":"python-docs","language":"python","kind":"crawl","seed":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/"},{"tool":"pep8","language":"python","kind":"crawl","seed":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/"},{"tool":"mdn-js","language":"javascript","kind":"crawl","seed":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/"},{"tool":"ts-handbook","language":"typescript","kind":"crawl","seed":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/"},{"tool":"effective-go","language":"go","kind":"crawl","seed":"https://go.dev/doc/effective_go"},{"tool":"java-tutorial","language":"java","kind":"crawl","seed":"https://docs.oracle.com/javase/tutorial/java/"},{"tool":"ruby-docs","language":"ruby","kind":"crawl","seed":"https://docs.ruby-lang.org/en/master/"},{"tool":"cppreference-c","language":"c","kind":"crawl","seed":"https://en.cppreference.com/c"},{"tool":"cppreference","language":"cpp","kind":"crawl","seed":"https://en.cppreference.com/cpp"},{"tool":"bash-manual","language":"bash","kind":"crawl","s